 fragment form (`#/a`) is not supported.
 
 Run the tests with `npm test` (Node 22.18 or later, which runs TypeScript directly).
+
+## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, applies a JSON Patch (an array of
+`add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test` operations) and returns the resulting document.
+Neither argument is mutated, and the patch is atomic: on failure it throws and returns nothing.
+
+It throws an `Error` when the patch is invalid (not an array, unknown `op`, missing or mistyped
+`path`, `from` or `value`, invalid pointer) or when an operation fails: target that does not resolve,
+array position out of range or not canonical, `move` into its own child, `test` mismatch. `-` is
+accepted only as the last token of an `add`/`copy`/`move` target. `remove` with the empty path is
+rejected, since the result would not be a JSON value. `test` compares objects regardless of member
+order. Pointers follow the rules of `resolvePointer` above.
